Z||000008||frontal lobe||11-15-2000||01:40 PM||||If they fly in your area, southwest airlines or ata airlines usually have very good rates.  You could check their websites.||||reg||1
Z||000009||william_thorniii||11-15-2000||04:38 PM||||The number one rule in this area is to check on them out of Columbus and Indy.  Cinci is the most expensive and Dayton is inbetween.  Try the oddballs, Comair (now owned by Delta), SW etc.  Let me know if you need a ride to Columbus/Indy.  I could use a road trip anyway.  I found when researching my honeymoon that travel agents could get the best prices but probably not in this short time.  Another tip that I have heard is that you could call the airline and ask for their lowest fare to your destination.  Sometimes they will give you a good price since if you don't buy from them, they will most likely have an empty seat.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
